    "enforcement": {
      "word": "ENFORCEMENT",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "The act of enforcing; compulsion. He that contendeth against these enforcements may easily master or resist them. Sir W. Raleigh. Confess 't was hers, and by what rough enforcement You got it from her. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A giving force to; a putting in execution. Enforcement of strict military discipline. Palfrey.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "That which enforces, constraints, gives force, authority, or effect to; constraint; force applied. The rewards and punishment of another life, which the Almighty has established as the enforcements of his law. Locke.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
